---
title: Proposition 6
---
order: 6
---
short_label: XI.6
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two straight lines are at right angles to the same plane, then the straight lines are parallel.
----
proof:

Let the two straight lines *AB* and *CD* be at right angles to the plane of reference.

I say that *AB* is parallel to *CD.*

Let them meet the plane of reference at the points *B* and *D.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="260" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.6 diagram" src="propXI6.gif"/></noscript>
